  "id": "at-risk-mental-states",
  "term": "at-risk mental states",
  "definition": "At-risk mental states are clinical states in which a person is identified as having an increased risk of developing psychosis, often before full psychotic symptoms are present. The term is used in early detection and prevention work because this risk phase can include subthreshold symptoms and may precede a first psychotic episode.",
